Attribute VB_Name = "TEST_Cases"

Option Explicit
Option Private Module

'
'==============================================================================
' MODULE: TEST_Cases
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' PURPOSE
'   The cases suite of the workbook's tests: every registered test case of
'   the project's calculations, as a case of TEST_Harness that types the
'   test case's inputs on the input sheets, runs the calculation through
'   RunSSA_Silent and compares every expected output with the cell that
'   holds it. GENERATED by tools/prototype/case_suite.py from
'   tests/fixtures/ and tests/expected/: do not edit it; change the test
'   case and write the module again.
'
' WHY THIS EXISTS
'   The inputs and the expected values of the test cases are data files; the
'   suite holds them as literals of this module, so that Excel reads no file
'   and the calculation is checked in the workbook itself.
'
' INPUTS
'   None at module level
'
' RETURNS
'   Nothing at module level
'
' BEHAVIOR
'   Gives three entry points:
'     - RunCaseTests is the documented test entry point
'     - Test_RunCases runs the same suite and returns its result line where
'       a caller cannot read an error, as tools/devbuild/lo_macro.py
'     - CertifyCases certifies the run and saves its log, its results and
'       its certification log as evidence of an Excel run
'
'   Each case replaces the inputs of the workbook with those of its test
'   case: the reporting date and currency, the regime and the total own
'   funds, the FX table, the option charges, the four position sheets and
'   the month ends of Eligibility. It rewrites the output sheets through
'   RunSSA_Silent, puts back the inputs the workbook had, on the success and
'   the error path, and asserts it. It clears the output sheets when it puts
'   the inputs back.
'
' ERROR POLICY
'   As TEST_Harness.EndRun: a run that does not pass raises ERR_TEST_FAILED,
'   or the unexpected error that escaped the runner. A refused start raises
'   TEST_Harness.ERR_TEST_DIRTY_START. An unexpected error inside a case is
'   recorded as a failure of that case, and the run continues. Test_RunCases
'   contains those errors; CertifyCases records them, saves the log, and
'   raises only when the certification did not pass.
'
' DEPENDENCIES
'   TEST_Harness; M_Main, CORE_Config and CORE_Util; the workbook's names
'   and sheets.
'
'   Reference: Each expected value, its class and its tolerance are those of
'   the test case's file in tests/expected/
'   (docs/methodology/TEST_CASES.md).
'
' NOTES
'   Option Explicit requires explicit declarations. Option Private Module
'   keeps the entry points out of the workbook's external surface and the
'   tests inside this project. Never part of the production import set.
'
'   State ownership: owns the copy of the inputs a case keeps while it runs,
'   their values and their formulas (mRows, mKept and mFormulas).
'
'   Usage: in a development workbook, type TEST_Cases.RunCaseTests in the
'   Immediate window. To record an Excel run, type
'       TEST_Cases.CertifyCases "<folder>", "<checkout>\tests\fixtures"
'   (INSTALLATION.md, Recording an Excel run).
'
'   Compatibility: Excel VBA; also runs under LibreOffice's VBA mode through
'   the tools of tools/devbuild/, which is never Excel evidence.
'
'   Author: Daniele Penza
'
' UPDATED
'   2026-11-21
'==============================================================================

'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' PRIVATE CONSTANTS
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    'A complete run starts every case and evaluates every assertion once
    Private Const SUITE_NAME          As String = "cases"   'Name of the suite in its log
    Private Const EXPECTED_CASES      As Long = 38          'Cases a complete run starts
    Private Const EXPECTED_ASSERTIONS As Long = 843         'Assertions a complete run evaluates

    'The inputs a test case replaces (InputArea)
    Private Const INPUT_AREAS   As Long = 14    'Areas kept and put back
    Private Const INPUT_ROWS    As Long = 500   'Fewest rows of a position sheet kept

    'Where a result per currency is found
    Private Const SEARCH_ROWS   As Long = 60    'Rows searched under a header
    Private Const FX_BLOCK_CODE As Long = 1     'Buckets FX block: currency
    Private Const FX_BLOCK_NET  As Long = 5     'Buckets FX block: net position

'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' PRIVATE STATE
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Private mRows(1 To 4)       As Long     'Rows of each position sheet kept
    Private mKept(1 To 14)      As Variant  'What each input area held: values
    Private mFormulas(1 To 14)  As Variant  'What each input area held: formulas


'
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
'
'                                 ENTRY POINTS
'
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
'

Public Sub RunCaseTests()

'
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
'                                RUN CASES SUITE
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' PURPOSE
'   Run the cases suite. A passing run ends with
'   RESULT=PASS; suite=cases; operation=PASS; completeness=COMPLETE;
'   cases=38; assertions=843; failures=0; cleanup=PASS; recovery=NONE.
'
' WHY THIS EXISTS
'   The documented entry point of the suite: it raises when the run does not
'   pass, as TEST_Harness.EndRun does.
'
' INPUTS
'   None
'
' RETURNS
'   Nothing
'
' BEHAVIOR
'   Calls RunSuite, which runs every case between BeginRun and EndRun.
'
' ERROR POLICY
'   As TEST_Harness.EndRun: raises when the run does not pass.
'
' DEPENDENCIES
'   RunSuite; TEST_Harness
'
' NOTES
'   Replaces the inputs for each case and puts them back; leaves the output
'   sheets cleared.
'
' UPDATED
'   2026-11-19
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------

'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' RUN SUITE
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    'Run every case, which raises when the run does not pass
        RunSuite

End Sub

Public Function Test_RunCases() As String

'
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
'                             RUN CASES FOR RESULT
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' PURPOSE
'   Run the cases suite for a caller that reads a result and not an error.
'
' WHY THIS EXISTS
'   A caller that cannot read an error, as tools/devbuild/lo_macro.py, still
'   needs the outcome of the run.
'
' INPUTS
'   None
'
' RETURNS
'   The RESULT line of the run, as TEST_Harness.LastResult gives it.
'
' BEHAVIOR
'   Runs the suite with the error of the run suppressed, then returns the
'   result line that TEST_Harness keeps.
'
' ERROR POLICY
'   Contains the error of a run that does not pass, or of a refused start:
'   the result line says so.
'
' DEPENDENCIES
'   RunSuite; TEST_Harness (LastResult)
'
' NOTES
'   State as RunCaseTests.
'
' UPDATED
'   2026-11-19
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------

'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' RUN SUITE
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    'Contain the error of a run that does not pass or of a refused start
        On Error Resume Next
        RunSuite
        On Error GoTo 0

'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' RETURN RESULT
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    'Return the result line of the run
        Test_RunCases = TEST_Harness.LastResult()

End Function

Public Sub CertifyCases( _
    ByVal Folder As String, _
    ByVal Fixtures As String)
'
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
'                              CERTIFY CASES SUITE
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' PURPOSE
'   Certify the cases suite's run as evidence of an Excel run: run it, save
'   its log as cases.log and its results as cases-results.json, and write
'   cases-certification.log.
'
' WHY THIS EXISTS
'   Evidence of an Excel run is its log, its results and its certification
'   log; this entry point makes the three files from one run.
'
' INPUTS
'   Folder
'     String: an existing folder for the files, without a trailing
'     separator.
'
'   Fixtures
'     String: the full path of tests/fixtures/ in the checkout. Not read,
'     because the inputs are in this module; taken so that every
'     certification entry point has the same two arguments.
'
' RETURNS
'   Nothing
'
' BEHAVIOR
'   Begins the certification, runs the suite with its error recorded and not
'   raised, saves the log, certifies the run, saves the results and ends the
'   certification.
'
' ERROR POLICY
'   The error of the run is recorded, not raised, so that the log is always
'   saved. Raises ERR_TEST_FAILED after writing the certification log when
'   the certification did not pass. An error of BeginCertification, SaveLog
'   or SaveResults propagates; run TEST_Harness.ResetTests before trying
'   again.
'
' DEPENDENCIES
'   RunSuite; TEST_Harness (BeginCertification, SaveLog, Echo, CertifyRun,
'   SaveResults, EndCertification)
'
' NOTES
'   State as RunCaseTests.
'
' UPDATED
'   2026-11-19
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------

'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' DECLARE
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Dim RunErrorNumber      As Long     'Error that ended the run; 0 for none
    Dim RunErrorDescription As String   'Its description

'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' BEGIN CERTIFICATION
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    'Start the certification of the suite
        TEST_Harness.BeginCertification SUITE_NAME

'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' RUN SUITE
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    'Run the suite and keep the error that ended it, so that the log is saved
        On Error Resume Next
        RunSuite
        RunErrorNumber = Err.Number
        RunErrorDescription = Err.Description
        On Error GoTo 0

'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' SAVE LOG
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    'Save the log and say where it is
        TEST_Harness.SaveLog Folder & "\cases.log"
        TEST_Harness.Echo "SAVED=" & Folder & "\cases.log; mode=NORMAL; error=" & _
            CStr(RunErrorNumber) & IIf(RunErrorNumber = 0, vbNullString, " " & RunErrorDescription)

'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' CERTIFY RUN
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    'Certify the normal run with the error that ended it
        TEST_Harness.CertifyRun "NORMAL", True, RunErrorNumber, RunErrorDescription

'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' SAVE RESULTS
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    'Save the results the cases recorded
        TEST_Harness.SaveResults Folder & "\cases-results.json"

'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' END CERTIFICATION
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    'Write the certification log, which raises when the certification failed
        TEST_Harness.EndCertification Folder & "\cases-certification.log"

End Sub

'
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
'
'                                    RUNNER
'
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
'

Private Sub RunSuite()

'
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
'                                   RUN CASES
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' PURPOSE
'   Run every case in a fixed order between BeginRun and EndRun.
'
' WHY THIS EXISTS
'   The three entry points run the suite the same way: the order of the
'   cases and the report of the run are in one place.
'
' INPUTS
'   None
'
' RETURNS
'   Nothing
'
' BEHAVIOR
'   Begins the run with the number of cases and of assertions it expects,
'   lets the suite write the sheets, calls every case in a fixed order and
'   ends the run with the error that escaped a case, if any.
'
' ERROR POLICY
'   An error escaping a case handler is passed to EndRun, which reports it
'   and re-raises it unchanged. BeginRun's refusal propagates directly.
'
' DEPENDENCIES
'   TEST_Harness (BeginRun, EndRun); AllowWritingToSheets; every Case
'   procedure of this module; the constants SUITE_NAME, EXPECTED_CASES and
'   EXPECTED_ASSERTIONS
'
' NOTES
'   None
'
' UPDATED
'   2026-11-19
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------

'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' DECLARE
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Dim ErrNumber       As Long     'Runner error number; 0 for none
    Dim ErrSource       As String   'Runner error source
    Dim ErrDescription  As String   'Runner error description

'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' BEGIN RUN
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    'Begin the run; a refused start raises here, before the handler is on
        TEST_Harness.BeginRun SUITE_NAME, "NORMAL", EXPECTED_CASES, EXPECTED_ASSERTIONS

'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' RUN CASES
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    'Keep an error that escapes a case, to report it at the end of the run
        On Error GoTo RunFailed
    'Let the suite write the sheets of the workbook
        AllowWritingToSheets
    'Run every case, in a fixed order
        CaseBcbs119C2MaturityMethod
        CaseIllustrativeCoBook
        CaseIllustrativeCoMatchedPositions
        CaseIllustrativeCrrAfterTransitionalEndDate
        CaseIllustrativeCrrFxAboveDeMinimis
        CaseIllustrativeCrrFxDeMinimisLimit
        CaseIllustrativeCrrIrSpecificRisk
        CaseIllustrativeCrrMaturityMethodC2
        CaseIllustrativeCrrSampleEquity
        CaseIllustrativeCrrSampleRequirement
        CaseIllustrativeCrrTransitionalEndDate
        CaseIllustrativeEligibilityBaselRegime
        CaseIllustrativeEligibilityEvents
        CaseIllustrativeEligibilityLimits
        CaseIllustrativeEligibilitySampleMonths
        CaseIllustrativeEqBook
        CaseIllustrativeEqMatchedPositions
        CaseIllustrativeFxBook
        CaseIllustrativeFxOneSidedPositions
        CaseIllustrativeInvalidCoPositions
        CaseIllustrativeInvalidCrrIrPositions
        CaseIllustrativeInvalidEligibilityMonths
        CaseIllustrativeInvalidEqPositions
        CaseIllustrativeInvalidFxPositions
        CaseIllustrativeInvalidIrPositions
        CaseIllustrativeIrBook
        CaseIllustrativeIrSpecificRiskMaturityLimits
        CaseIllustrativeIrTimeBandLimits
        CaseIllustrativeOptionCharges
        CaseIllustrativeRequirementFxAndOptionsOnly
        CaseIllustrativeSampleCommodities
        CaseIllustrativeSampleEquity
        CaseIllustrativeSampleFx
        CaseIllustrativeSampleIrGeneralMarketRisk
        CaseIllustrativeSampleIrSpecificRisk
        CaseIllustrativeSampleRequirement
        CaseMar4027VerticalDisallowance
        CaseMar4061Table9

'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' END RUN
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Finish:
    'Stop catching errors before the run ends
        On Error GoTo 0
    'End the run: it raises when the run did not pass
        TEST_Harness.EndRun ErrNumber, ErrSource, ErrDescription

'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' EXIT PROCEDURE
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    'Leave before the error handler
        Exit Sub

'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' ERROR HANDLER
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
RunFailed:
    'Keep the error that escaped a case
        ErrNumber = Err.Number
        ErrSource = Err.Source
        ErrDescription = Err.Description
    'Go on to the end of the run, which reports the error
        Resume Finish

End Sub

